    "recommendations": "Ensuring the single access point and extended driveway remain clear of parked vehicles and stored materials could meaningfully improve apparatus entry and positioning during an emergency response. Marking or identifying the driveway entry from the street frontage may assist responding units in locating the property quickly under low-visibility or nighttime conditions. Maintaining a designated staging area near the front of the property would support simultaneous access by multiple response units. Relocating or organizing materials within the outdoor storage area to avoid encroachment on travel corridors near the detached structure could facilitate responder movement around the property perimeter, partially offsetting the limited rear access identified from the aerial view."
