    "recommendations": "Reducing the density of brush and shrubs immediately surrounding the structure and creating greater separation between vegetation and the building perimeter could meaningfully improve defensible space and reduce fuel continuity near the improvements. Where heavy brush and dense shrub cover exist in close proximity to the structure, thinning or removing surface fuels in the immediate perimeter zone would support suppression efforts and improve conditions for firefighters working around the building. Managing vegetation along the length of the driveway, including trimming encroaching shrubs and maintaining adequate vertical and lateral clearance, would support firefighter access and evacuation along what appears to be the sole access route serving the property. Preserving any existing open terrain as a natural fuel break and avoiding new plantings that could increase vegetative density within the structure perimeter could further reduce fuel continuity and improve long-term wildfire resilience."
